1: // trap_sm120.cpp - XSched level-3 trap backend for Blackwell sm120 (Linux).
2: //
3: // Mechanism (validated in test/sm120_l3_trap_v2, FINDINGS_ZH.md v2.0):
4: //   * the live driver .text.traphandler (arena base + 0x15f0f00) is patched at
5: //     +0x390 with CALL.ABS to a cave in the slot-20 object (+0xA00);
6: //   * the cave is a harmless return stub by default.  To preempt, it is
7: //     rewritten to "redirect the saved TRAP_RETURN_PC to an EXIT trampoline"
8: //     (cave+0x70).  The handler finishes restoring the trap state first, so the
9: //     warp exits cleanly and the context survives;
10: //   * an external agent holds a 0x83de session bound to {app client, KGO} and
11: //     sends 0x83de0317{0,0} when asked; the app grants it access with the
12: //     NV01_ROOT 0xd04 inherited-share policy (late grant works).
13: //
14: // The app and agent talk over a POSIX shm control block (trap_sm120_shm.h).
